125 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 65 0 R/E(        The Hotel Reservation & Check-In System is a Java Swing\205based desktop application developed for the CS342 course. The project aims to automate hotel front-desk operations by providing an efficient system for managing room reservations, guest check-in and check-out, billing, and payments.)/Pg 10 0 R/K[0 1]>>
endobj

126 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 65 0 R/E(        The application follows the MVC architecture and integrates with a relational database using JDBC to ensure organized data management and persistence. It supports role-based authentication for receptionists and managers, along with input validation and exception handling to prevent booking conflicts and invalid operations.)/Pg 10 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

127 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 65 0 R/E(Introduction)/Pg 10 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

128 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 65 0 R/E(PAGE 03)/Pg 10 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

129 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 66 0 R/E( PAGE 04)/Pg 11 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

130 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 66 0 R/E( Application Overview)/Pg 11 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

131 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 66 0 R/E(Hotel Reservation System is a desktop-based application designed to support the daily operations of a hotel in an organized and efficient manner. It manages the complete reservation lifecycle, beginning with guest registration and reservation creation, continuing through check-in and check-out processes, and concluding with billing and payment tracking.)/Pg 11 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

132 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 66 0 R/E(The application enables hotel staff to create and manage guest records and reservations while ensuring accurate tracking of room availability and room statuses, including Available, Occupied, and Cleaning Required. This functionality provides real-time visibility into room usage and operational readiness.)/Pg 11 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

133 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 66 0 R/E(During the check-in and check-out processes, the system enforces strict status validation to ensure that reservations and rooms follow the correct operational workflow. This helps prevent conflicts such as double bookings and invalid room assignments.)/Pg 11 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

134 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 66 0 R/E(At check-out, the system generates detailed and itemized invoices that include room charges, additional services, taxes, and applicable discounts. Discounts are retrieved from the database and applied according to predefined rules, allowing the system to accurately calculate the final payable amount.)/Pg 11 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

135 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 66 0 R/E(The billing module supports partial and multiple payments by allowing more than one payment record to be associated with a single invoice. This enables flexible payment handling while maintaining accurate financial records.)/Pg 11 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

136 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 66 0 R/E(In addition, the system provides reporting features such as income summaries, enabling management to analyze financial performance by comparing total invoiced amounts with received payments, including the impact of applied discounts. By integrating all system components with a centralized database, the application ensures data accuracy, consistency, and efficient hotel operations.)/Pg 11 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

137 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 67 0 R/E(GUI Elements)/Pg 12 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

138 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 67 0 R/E(PAGE 05 )/Pg 12 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

139 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 67 0 R/E(The interface is designed to be simple, intuitive, and easy to navigate, allowing hotel staff to perform daily operations efficiently.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

140 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 67 0 R/E(The system includes multiple screens such as Login, Manager Dashboard, Reservation Management, Room Management, Check-In, Check-Out, Invoice View, Payment Management, and Discount Management. Each screen is organized using standard Swing components including buttons, text fields, labels, combo boxes, tables, and dialog windows.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

141 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 67 0 R/E(Tables \(JTable\) are used extensively to display structured data such as reservations, rooms, invoices, payments, and discounts. These tables support row selection, enabling users to view, update, or delete records easily.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

142 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 67 0 R/E(Dialog windows \(JDialog\) are used for focused tasks such as check-in, check-out, invoice viewing, and payment entry, ensuring that users complete one operation at a time without confusion.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

143 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 67 0 R/E(Buttons are clearly labeled and styled consistently across the application to guide users through actions such as creating records, confirming operations, generating invoices, and completing payments. Confirmation and warning dialogs are displayed for critical actions to prevent accidental data loss.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

144 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 67 0 R/E(Overall, the GUI design emphasizes clarity, consistency, and usability, ensuring that hotel staff can interact with the system efficiently with minimal training.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

