endobj

290 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 81 0 R/E(        The connection is established using the DriverManager class, which opens a connection to the SQLite database file located in the project resources directory \(hotel.db\). The database URL follows the SQLite JDBC format:)/Pg 26 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

291 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 81 0 R/E(                            jdbc:sqlite:src/main/resources/hotel.db)/Pg 26 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

292 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 81 0 R/E(        The getConnection\(\) method provides a reusable way for Data Access Object \(DAO\) classes to access the database. Each DAO class \(such as ReservationDAO, RoomDAO, and GuestDAO\) is responsible for executing SQL operations related to a specific entity, including retrieving, inserting, updating, and deleting records.)/Pg 26 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

293 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 81 0 R/E(        This design separates database logic from the user interface, centralizes database operations, and improves maintainability and code organization.)/Pg 26 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

294 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 81 0 R/E(        To verify and inspect the database content, DB Browser for SQLite was used. This tool helped ensure that data was stored correctly and that database operations were executed as expected.)/Pg 26 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

