299 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 83 0 R/E(Database-related exceptions, such as connection failures or SQL execution errors, are caught and handled gracefully. When an error occurs, the system displays clear error messages using dialog boxes, allowing users to understand the issue without exposing technical details.)/Pg 28 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

300 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 83 0 R/E(User input validation is performed before executing critical operations to prevent common runtime errors. This includes checking for empty fields, invalid numeric values, incorrect date formats, and invalid discount codes. If validation fails, informative warning messages are shown to guide the user in correcting the input.)/Pg 28 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

301 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 83 0 R/E(Transactional operations, such as check-out and invoice generation, are protected using database transactions. In case of failure, changes are rolled back to maintain data consistency between reservations, rooms, invoices, and payments.)/Pg 28 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

302 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 83 0 R/E(Through these mechanisms, the system ensures reliability, data integrity, and a smooth user experience even when errors occur.)/Pg 28 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

