326 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 85 0 R/E(In conclusion, the Hotel Reservation and Check-In System successfully demonstrates the application of core software engineering principles in designing and implementing a real-world hotel management solution. The system provides essential functionalities such as room reservations, guest management, check-in and check-out operations, waitlist handling, and billing support, ensuring an organized and efficient workflow for hotel staff.)/Pg 30 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

327 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 85 0 R/E(By integrating a relational database, the system ensures data consistency, persistence, and reliability across all operations. The use of a layered architecture with clearly separated models, data access objects \(DAOs\), and user interface components enhances maintainability and scalability. Additionally, validation mechanisms and exception handling improve system robustness by preventing invalid bookings and handling conflicting reservation scenarios.)/Pg 30 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

328 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 85 0 R/E(Overall, this project reflects a practical understanding of object-oriented design, database integration, and GUI development using Java Swing. It effectively simulates real-world hotel operations and serves as a strong foundation for future enhancements such as online reservations, payment gateway integration, and advanced reporting features.)/Pg 30 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

